# Baseline Audit Report

> Install-time state assessment generated by the `BASELINE-AUDIT` meta-skill. Establishes the "before" picture against which all future progress measures.
>
> **Default visibility:** gitignored. Contains findings and threat surface information valuable to attackers if exposed.

- **Date generated:** YYYY-MM-DD
- **Framework version:** [TGF version]
- **Project:** [Name from PROJECT-CONTEXT]
- **Audit type:** [Greenfield (skipped — no code) | Brownfield (full seven-phase) | Recurring lite | Pre-launch | Post-incident]

---

## Executive Summary

[High-level state assessment, top 3 risks identified, top 3 strengths. Three to five paragraphs.]

---

## Phase 1 — Inventory

[What exists — stack components, dependencies (with versions), file structure, build/deploy tooling, line counts by area, primary languages, environment variable patterns observed.]

## Phase 2 — Configuration Audit

[Authentication setup, authorization patterns, secrets management approach, CI/CD configuration, deployment patterns, observability setup. Patterns flagged for follow-up.]

## Phase 3 — Code Quality Scan

[TypeScript strictness (or equivalent), error handling patterns, test coverage if detectable, file size distributions, evidence of layering, naming consistency, import patterns.]

## Phase 4 — Security Baseline

[Authentication flow review, authorization check coverage, input validation patterns, output encoding, webhook handling, file upload security, CSP/security headers, dependency vulnerability scan results.]

## Phase 5 — Threat Surface Mapping

[Where untrusted input enters. Where sensitive data lives. What crosses what trust boundaries. Existing controls at boundaries. Project-specific zone map if applicable.]

## Phase 6 — Compliance Gap

[Comparison of current state to PROJECT-CONTEXT compliance posture. Gaps identified for each applicable regime (GDPR, CCPA, HIPAA, PCI-DSS, SOC 2, etc.).]

## Phase 7 — Synthesis

